NoQuarter EoTS (Eye of the Storm) - CHANGES
===========================================

NoQuarter EoTS (short: NQ EoTS) is an unofficial, community-maintained
continuation of No Quarter. It is a modified version (an "Extension")
of No Quarter by the No Quarter Mod Team and is distributed under the
No Quarter Mod Team's Modified Reciprocal Public License 1.1
(see License.txt). It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
original No Quarter Mod Team. All credit for No Quarter itself belongs
to them and to its contributors.

Based on:    No Quarter SVN trunk, revision 5758 (2012-04-16)
Maintainer:  Hawkeye
Source code: https://github.com/DL-LAM/NoQuarter-1.3.1-32-bit-and-64-bit-
Contact:     NoQuarter Discord - https://discord.gg/c5yREDTt5

All changes listed below are by Hawkeye unless stated otherwise.

Finding a change in the source code
-----------------------------------
Modified code is marked with comment tags of the form
[NQ 1.3.1 - <Area>], for example [NQ 1.3.1 - Security],
[NQ 1.3.1 - Widescreen] or [NQ 1.3.1 - Audit C1]. Search the source
for the tag to find the change. Changes made after the rename to
NoQuarter EoTS use tags of the form [EoTS 1.0 - <Area>]. The audit fixes (tags "Audit <ID>")
are listed individually in docs/AUDIT_2026-09-25.md. The full history
of the git era (2026-09-01 onward) is in the repository's commit log.


EoTS 1.0.7b (beta)                                                  2026-09-30
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Renamed from NoQuarter 1.3.1 to NoQuarter EoTS ("Eye of the Storm") and
reversioned to 1.0.7b; the "b7" matches the last 1.3.1 beta, and the game
itself is the same as 1.3.1b7.
- New name and version on the loading screen, in the in-game and NQ options
  menus, in console help, crash logs, server check messages and the default
  server_motd0. (src/game/bg_public.h, src/game/g_main.c, src/game/g_crash.c,
  src/cgame/cg_loadpanel.c, src/cgame/cg_crash.c, src/cgame/cg_consolecmds.c,
  src/cgame/nq_server_help.h, scripts/package_release.py)
- pk3s renamed to nqeots_v1.0.7b.pk3 and nqeots_b_v1.0.7b.pk3. The server warns
  when old nq_v1.3.x / nq_b_v1.3.x pk3s are still installed.
- mod_version is "NQ EoTS 1.0.7b"; mod_url points to this project's source
  repository instead of the original team's site.
- Not changed: the mod folder and gamename stay "nq", and Omni-bot is still
  told the mod version is 1.3.1.
- README: added the derived-from statement, corrected the license section
  (No Quarter is under the No Quarter Mod Team's Modified RPL 1.1, not the
  GPL) and corrected the credits.


1.3.1b7 (beta)                                         2026-09-26 - 2026-09-29
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Engine / platform
- Windows 64-bit servers load Omni-bot from omnibot_et_x64.dll. Fixed a
  crash in the Omni-bot loader's error reporting (OB_ShowLastError) that
  shut 64-bit Windows servers down at startup.
  (Omnibot/Common/BotLoadLibrary.cpp)
- Fixed the Omni-bot "Looking for" log message on Linux (missing format
  argument). (Omnibot/Common/BotLoadLibrary.cpp)
- Linux: LuaSQL and SQLite are compiled into qagame (NQ_BUILTIN_LUASQL) and
  registered as a preloaded Lua module, so require("luasql.sqlite3") works
  on Linux servers without extra library files. The previous separate
  Linux sqlite3.so / liblua5.1.so files were empty and never worked.
  (src/game/g_lua.c, scripts/build_linux.py)

Build and packaging
- Windows builds no longer embed the builder's folder paths (/d1trimfile,
  /PDBALTPATH:%_PDB%). Linux builds use -ffile-prefix-map, no debug info,
  and stripped binaries. (src/CMakeLists.txt, scripts/build_linux.py)
- Release packaging picks the newest build folder, ships the Windows LuaSQL
  driver as lualibs/luasql/sqlite3.dll, and no longer ships the empty Linux
  library stubs. (scripts/package_release.py)
- Added CMakeSettings.json for Visual Studio "Open Folder" builds.
- Unified binary pk3 (nq_b_v1.3.1b7.pk3) rebuilt with all eight client
  binaries (Windows x86/x64, Linux i386/x86_64).

Configuration and scripts (release package)
- noquarter.cfg: added g_log, g_logSync, g_logChat, g_tyranny,
  sv_allowDownload and g_discordURL; referee lockout cvars in all sample
  configs; docs/noquarter_commented.txt documents each one.
- WolfAdmin: new !discord / !bug command (shows g_discordURL for bug
  reports), new !resetmyxp for standalone mode (permission resetxp_self),
  a Discord banner, and pip/rocket permission constants.
- xpsave.lua: database path taken from fs_homepath/fs_game instead of a
  hardcoded path; !setxp respects WolfAdmin admin levels in standalone
  mode; removed hardcoded admin GUIDs.
- Disabled a bot XP-reset hook in WolfAdmin's greetings module.
- Removed the unfinished shrubbot_fun.lua from the release.

Documentation
- README, installation guide, developer knowledge base and agent notes
  updated (Lua/SQLite file layout, build notes, solved issues).
- Added SECURITY.md (private vulnerability reporting).


1.3.1 source audit                                                  2026-09-25
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Security, stability and 64-bit fixes from a full review of the game code.
Each item is tagged [NQ 1.3.1 - Audit <ID>] in the source and described in
docs/AUDIT_2026-09-25.md. Highlights:
- C1: fireteam kick/propose on yourself could shut the server down.
- C2: map-vote IDs were not range-checked (write outside the vote table).
- H1: IPv6 players were refused ("Bad userinfo").
- H2: Lua et.G_LogPrint used its text as a printf format string.
- H3: XP save file path built from an unvalidated cl_guid (path traversal).
- H4: full shrubbot tables wrote past the end of the array; readconfig
  stopped reading mid-file.
- M1-M10: UTF-8 names accepted, exact IP ban matching, GUID-less ban fix,
  IPv4 filter parser, portable 32/64-bit XP save files, Lua string
  ownership, !unban bounds, props NULL check, bounded va(), info-string
  fixes.
- L1-L9: assorted bounds checks and 64-bit printf fixes.
- Linux 64-bit (LP64) math fixes: Q_rsqrt, SinCos, COM_Bit* and long-based
  string hashes.
- Map scripts: unknown map-script actions/events are skipped with a
  warning instead of shutting the server down (maps made for other mods).
  [NQ 1.3.1 - MapScript]


1.3.1b6 / b7 packaging                                   2026-09-20 - 2026-09-22
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Unified pk3 layout: one asset pk3 (nq_v1.3.1bX.pk3) and one binary pk3
  (nq_b_v1.3.1bX.pk3) with the client binaries for every platform, so
  32-bit and 64-bit players can share a pure server.
- Version bumped to 1.3.1b7; build scripts and documentation updated.
- Removed 778 leftover SVN metadata files from version control.


Security and widescreen hardening                        2026-09-15 - 2026-09-21
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- RCON and referee authentication: configurable lockout after repeated
  failed passwords (g_authFailures, g_authFailBanTime,
  g_authFailExpireTime), IPv6-safe address buffers.
- Lua subsystem and shrubbot bridge hardened against privilege escalation
  and memory corruption; format-string, bounds and pointer fixes across the
  game code. [NQ 1.3.1 - Security] / [NQ 1.3.1 - Bounds]
- NQKey stack buffer overflow fixed; IPv6 support in shrubbot bans.
- NULL client/entity guards in referee, vote, fireteam and multiview code;
  sv_fps division guards; Omni-bot interface bounds checks.
- Widescreen (16:9, 16:10, 21:9) UI and aspect-ratio overhaul: centered
  menus, main menu docked left, fullscreen backgrounds without gaps.
  [NQ 1.3.1 - Widescreen]
- Airstrike plane flyover animation fixed; center-print HUD text no longer
  overlaps the kill feed. [NQ 1.3.1 - Airstrike] / [NQ 1.3.1 - HUD]
- Linux server: Lua embedded statically, ORIGIN rpath, GCC inline symbol fix.
- Server configs and commented documentation updated for 1.3.1.
- Developer knowledge base and build documentation added.


1.3.1 initial work (before git history)                           to 2026-09-05
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes made to the r5758 source before and during the first git commits
(2026-09-01 import, 2026-09-05 release):
- 64-bit support for Windows (x64) and Linux (x86_64): pointer-safe
  syscalls in cgame, ui and qagame; 64-bit crash handlers; ET:Legacy
  OS-support flags and pk3 checks. [NQ 1.3.1 - Windows 64-bit] /
  [NQ 1.3.1 - Linux 64-bit] / [NQ 1.3.1 - Portability]
- Widescreen Hor+ field-of-view correction. [NQ 1.3.1 - Widescreen]
- Modernized intermission / debriefing screens (scoreboard, awards, stats
  and map-vote tabs) and a modern XP popup showing the reason for XP gains.
- Weapon icon color reflects the weapon's current state.
- Limbo panel default secondary-weapon selection updated for the soldier
  shotgun and akimbo pistols; soldier level 4+ SMG/shotgun secondary.
- Bounds checks for custom maps with more spawn points or objective
  triggers than the original limits.
- Map location file parsing rewritten (cg_localents.c).
- Omni-bot 0.93 integration.
- Asset fixes in the asset pk3: menus, right-side-up caduceus in
  meyer.shader, and CMYK JPEG textures converted so 32-bit clients no
  longer crash.


Third-party components included in the release
-----------------------------------------------
These keep their own licenses and are not covered by the No Quarter
license: Lua 5.1 (MIT), SQLite (public domain), LuaSQL (MIT),
WolfAdmin 1.2.1 by Timo 'Timothy' Smit (GPLv3), Omni-bot.


